style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-20T11:29:48-07:00","id":1560790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1560694-a-traditional-chinese-medicine-based-legacy?p=1560775#post1560775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">I think the attachments of prosthetics would be a Weaving. When designing the furnace lords, I was assuming that making or finding prosthetics of comparable quality to those of G\u00f6tz of the Iron Hand was not an easy thing when they were created. If I understood correctly, this offshoot has a greater focus on the chemistry side of alchemy, being more effective at creating medicine and adjusting the body's chemistry. Some possible ideas for Attainments:</span><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The reasoning behind the level 2 prosthetics attainment was that the animation part is done by the Remote control spell, and as long as there was no sensory feedback a conjunctional life 2 would be enough to make the object respond to the residual muscle movement of the stump instead of the mage will.<br /> Also i figured out that restoring a basic grip with crude prosthetics, like a wooden one built like a marionette part or a copper one more precise but frail, were not so hard to craft in that age (expecially for a Matter mage) and more than enough for a working paesant.<br /> <br /> About the attainments in general, yes your understanding is right and the focus is on improving general quality of lif with tools and drugs.<br /> I think that the attainment i ve posted are a good mix of healing and prevent harm, for the final attainment i wanted something that seems like a culmination of that attitude, a bless that the master gives to a community to ease their labor in order to focus on more phylosopical themes (and likely Awaken).<br /> <br /> So for the fifth attainment honing the form seems a good bless to enhance various professions (farmer, hunter, smith, even soldier) or simply general health.<br /> For the optional matter one i like the Crucible approach but i can t easily figure out what could work as a conjunctional life increasing of &quot;value&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}